If you have completed [conda installation tutorial](conda_installation.qmd), our first step would be to downalod data from public repositories. for this we have to install `sra-tools`

``` bash
conda activate wgs
```

``` bash 
conda install bioconda::sra-tools -y
```

Let's download the sequence files for _Aeromonas caviae_ `SRR31323044` from NCBI SRA database.

``` bash
prefetch --help 
# if it works move to next command
```

``` bash
prefetch SRR31323044
```
If the file is downloaded successfully, our step would to split files into two files, `R1/forward read` and `R2/reverence read`

``` bash
fasterq-dump SRR31323044/SRR31323044.sra --split-files --threads 8 
```
You will two files have been created as

- `SRR31323044_1.fastq`
- `SRR31323044_2.fastq`

Your step would be to run:
```
- FastQC        #quality check the raw reads 
- Trimmomatic   #trimming the raw reads
- Spades        #contigs generation from trimmed reads
- Quast         #quality check for the generated contigs
```
You can do it by yourself, I believe you gained enough cofidence to do all the analysis by yourself. Best wishes!!!












